From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Borja Tarraso <borja.tarraso@member.fsf.org>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] emacsclient: suppress ENOPROTOOPT noise from SO_RCVTIMEO on
 GNU/Hurd

* lib-src/emacsclient.c (set_local_socket): do not surface the
SO_RCVTIMEO setsockopt failure when errno is ENOPROTOOPT.  GNU/Hurd's
pflocal does not implement the option; the timeout is best-effort and
the warning is noise.  Other errors from setsockopt still surface so a
real failure on Linux is not masked.

Reported on Debian GNU/Hurd 0.9 with emacs 29.4 (glibc GLIBC_2.38):
every emacsclient invocation against a running emacs daemon prints

  /usr/bin/emacsclient.emacs: setsockopt: Protocol not available

once on stderr, then proceeds correctly (eval result on stdout, exit
code 0).  Confirmed via gdb break on setsockopt: arg shape
fd=3 level=65535 (SOL_SOCKET) optname=4102 (SO_RCVTIMEO).  pflocal
returns ENOPROTOOPT for this option; glibc's strerror text for it
on Hurd is "Protocol not available".
---
 lib-src/emacsclient.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib-src/emacsclient.c b/lib-src/emacsclient.c
--- a/lib-src/emacsclient.c
+++ b/lib-src/emacsclient.c
@@
   struct timeval tv;
   tv.tv_sec  = MINIBUF_WAIT_SECONDS;
   tv.tv_usec = 0;
-  if (setsockopt (s, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVTIMEO, &tv, sizeof tv) < 0)
-    message (true, "%s: setsockopt: %s\n", progname, strerror (errno));
+  /* GNU/Hurd's pflocal does not implement this option; the timeout
+     is best-effort, the warning is noise.  Suppress only the
+     ENOPROTOOPT case so a real failure on Linux still surfaces.  */
+  if (setsockopt (s, SOL_SOCKET, SO_RCVTIMEO, &tv, sizeof tv) < 0
+      && errno != ENOPROTOOPT)
+    message (true, "%s: setsockopt: %s\n", progname, strerror (errno));
--
